IO-15: accept [GROUNDWATER] rows with the 10 required fields

handle_groundwater() copied legacy's off-by-one: it reads seven required
numbers from tokens 3-9 and treats tokens 10-13 as optional, but rejected any
row with fewer than 11 tokens with ERROR 203. Require 10 tokens, as
IO-15_swmm530.patch does for 5.3.0.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-15_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/input/handlers/HydrologyHandler.cpp b/src/engine/input/handlers/HydrologyHandler.cpp
index 5035f36..d25d543 100644
--- a/src/engine/input/handlers/HydrologyHandler.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/input/handlers/HydrologyHandler.cpp
@@ -415,10 +415,10 @@ void handle_groundwater(SimulationContext& ctx, const std::vector<std::string>&
         auto tok = Tokenizer::tokenize(line);
         if (tok.empty()) continue;
         // Subcatch  Aquifer  Node  SurfEl  A1  B1  A2  B2  A3  Dsw  [Egwt  Ebot  Wgw  Umc]
-        // Legacy gwater.c gwater_readGroundwaterParams requires >= 11 tokens;
-        // fewer is ERR_ITEMS (too few items). v6 formerly skipped short rows
-        // silently, so a truncated row ran instead of being rejected.
-        if (tok.size() < 11) {
+        // The 10 fields up to Dsw are required; fewer is ERR_ITEMS (too few
+        // items). v6 formerly skipped short rows silently, so a truncated row
+        // ran instead of being rejected.
+        if (tok.size() < 10) {
             ctx.errors.push_back(format_error(ERR_ITEMS, ""));
             continue;
         }
